    "answer": {
      "short": "$15$ and $18$.",
      "worked": "Let the smaller number be $x$. The larger number is $x+3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+x+3&=33\\\\2x+3&=33\\\\2x&=30\\\\x&=15\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe larger number is $15+3=18$. The numbers are $15$ and $18$.\n\nCheck: $18-15=3$ and $15+18=33$.",
